### Title

Install a plugin in an installer-protected base.

### Why

Users can install a plugin with the original installer freeze in place. An administrator can replace that freeze to block plugin installation.

### Platforms

- [ ] Windows
- [ ] macOS
- [ ] Linux

### Prerequisites

Use a disposable protected-base Miniconda or Anaconda Distribution installation running this build of conda. Choose a plugin from the installer's channels.

### Steps

1. Activate a different environment. Run `conda plugins install -n base PACKAGE` with the plugin package name.
2. Run `conda plugins list` to see whether the running conda loads the plugin.
3. Empty the existing `conda-meta/frozen` file in base and repeat the install.

### Pass criteria

The first install succeeds without an override and conda lists the plugin. The second install reports that base is frozen.
